 "description": "The cybercrime group «Lazarus» (also known as Dark Seoul Gang/HIDDEN COBRA/Guardians of Peace), which has North Korean roots, is behind the major attacks, such as attack on the film company Sony Pictures Entertainment in 2014, the Bangladesh Bank heist on $81 million in February 2016 and compromise of several banks in Poland in February 2017. For the first time, the hacker group «Lazarus» was seen in the attacks against South Korean government in 2007. The victims of these criminals have become the people from South Korea, India, China, Brazil, Russia, Turkey, Mexico, Indonesia, Singapore and other countries. Lazarus was suspect in the attacks on the banks of Seoul, the media and military forces of South Korea.",
